      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nestordrod/{size}/2353_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-13T01:45:07.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I decided to try out Spite as a villain in the iPad app and found the whoel thing an exercise in frustration.</p><p>What made it even more annoying was what seems to be a bug in the game. The PL602 Compound Omicron card states \"The&nbsp;<em>first</em> time Spite would be dealt damage each turn, reduce that damage by H minus 2\" (emphasis mine).</p><p>What was happening, though, was that&nbsp;<em>all</em> attacks were being reduced, not just the first one. So all the heroes had to do at least 4 points of damage to even register against Spite, only to see it be erased the next time he hits a hero.</p><p>Pretty much makes the villain unplayable, in my opinion.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:13.737Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 0,
